## Bounded standalone graphics

The caller supplies only a safe companion path. Captions are escaped like other
renderer-owned text; no author TeX is executed. Image requests remain errors when
no asset adapter is supplied. Width is local to the current list/quote container.
Authored images retain the existing page-fitting behavior. Mermaid companions use
a separate box: it begins at the vector PDF's natural size, then shrinks only when
that box exceeds the local width or usable page height.

```ts : <<publication LaTeX code>>=+
function imageBlock(asset: PublicationAsset, resolve: (asset: PublicationAsset) => string): PandocBlock[] {
    const file = resolve(asset);
    if (!/^lit-assets-[a-f0-9]{64}\/[a-f0-9]{64}\.(png|jpg|pdf)$/.test(file)) {
        throw new Error('Image adapter must return a safe publication companion path');
    }
    if (Array.from(asset.caption).length > 4096) { throw new Error('Image caption exceeds 4096 characters'); }
    return [{ t: 'RawBlock', c: ['latex', asset.kind === 'mermaid'
        ? `\\LitDiagram{${file}}` : `\\LitImage{${file}}{${tex(asset.caption)}}`] }];
}
```

Measure the caption before sizing the graphic. The 24 pt reserve covers vertical
spacing and rounding; a caption that leaves no useful graphic space is an error,
not clipped text. Explicit boxes avoid paragraph baseline glue between the graphic
and caption. A final zero kern gives the complete box zero depth, so the page
builder can move it intact without losing its lower half to a centered baseline.
An explicit break opportunity permits a full-height image to leave a preceding
heading behind; a heading's keep-with-next penalty must not force the pair beyond
the page body. Percent line endings prevent macro formatting from consuming
horizontal space. EPS auto-conversion is disabled: supported assets never require
shell escape.

```ts : <<publication LaTeX template>>=+
function templateImageSettings(): string {
    return String.raw`\newsavebox{\LitCaptionBox}
\newsavebox{\LitDiagramBox}
\newlength{\LitImageHeight}
\newlength{\LitDiagramHeight}
\newcommand{\LitImage}[2]{\par\penalty0\addvspace{6pt}%
\begingroup
\sbox{\LitCaptionBox}{\parbox{\linewidth}{\small\raggedright #2\par}}%
\setlength{\LitImageHeight}{\dimexpr\textheight-\ht\LitCaptionBox-\dp\LitCaptionBox-24pt\relax}%
\ifdim\LitImageHeight<24pt
  \PackageError{literate}{Image caption leaves no space for graphic}{Shorten the caption.}%
\else
  \noindent\vbox{\hbox to\linewidth{\hfil
    \includegraphics[width=\linewidth,height=\LitImageHeight,keepaspectratio]{#1}\hfil}%
    \kern6pt\nointerlineskip\hbox{${'\\usebox'}{\LitCaptionBox}}\kern0pt}%
\fi
\par\endgroup\addvspace{6pt}}
\newcommand{\LitDiagram}[1]{\par\penalty0\addvspace{6pt}%
\begingroup
\setlength{\LitDiagramHeight}{\dimexpr\textheight-12pt\relax}%
\sbox{\LitDiagramBox}{\includegraphics{#1}}%
\ifdim\wd\LitDiagramBox>\linewidth
  \sbox{\LitDiagramBox}{\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{#1}}%
\fi
\ifdim\dimexpr\ht\LitDiagramBox+\dp\LitDiagramBox\relax>\LitDiagramHeight
  \sbox{\LitDiagramBox}{\includegraphics[height=\LitDiagramHeight]{#1}}%
\fi
\noindent\vbox{\hbox to\linewidth{\hfil\usebox{\LitDiagramBox}\hfil}\kern0pt}%
\par\endgroup\addvspace{6pt}}`;
}
```

## Deliberate boundaries

Raw author markup, tables, Mermaid, inline images and unsupported links still fail
in `preparePandoc`; this is not yet a whole-project book exporter. Standalone
PNG/JPEG/PDF images are packaged by the CLI. No fonts are downloaded or TeX files compiled. The caller must install Latin
Modern, Monofur Nerd Font and Lilex Nerd Font (or supply safe family overrides or
portable companions), and the listed TeX packages. Missing glyphs remain compiler
errors/warnings to check, not a claim of universal Unicode coverage.

Prose escaping remains the trusted Pandoc writer's responsibility; inline and
ordinary block code are escaped by this renderer before conversion. Converters must
preserve trusted RawBlocks and RawInlines, without filters, external includes, or highlighting. The ignored `out/publication-renderer` harness
compiles rosepine-dawn, hermonica and flexoki-light A5 fixtures, including nested
containers, full references and long styled tokens. It retains logs, glyph traces,
link/bounds checks and previews. Headless tests cover every catalogue theme, but
all palettes, fonts, arbitrary container depths and pagination are not PDF-validated.
References introduce display-only line breaks; executable copying must use original
or tangled source. CLI adapters, heading identity, packaging,
transactions and generation belong to their separate integration slices.
